{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Example: Step responses",
  "exampleId": "block-step-responses",
  "description": "The step comes at 0.1 s. The filter (τ = 0.2 s) reaches 63 % at 0.3 s. The second-order block (ωn = 10 rad/s, ζ = 0.3) overshoots to 1.37 at 0.43 s and rings down. The integrator rises at 1 per second; the limited integrator rises the same way until it reaches its limit of 1 at 1.1 s and stops there. The delay repeats the step 0.3 s late. The derivative of a ramp with slope 2 is 2.",
  "duration": 2,
  "revision": 0,
  "blocks": [
